What this is, and what it was written against
---------------------------------------------

virglrs is a from-scratch Rust implementation of the virtio-gpu host renderer. It was written
against virglrenderer (https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/virgl/virglrenderer), which is MIT-licensed
and is itself derived from Mesa in many parts, and it is tested against it: the harness records
its goldens by running the same corpora through both.

virglrenderer's authors include Red Hat, Google, Collabora and the Mesa contributors. This
implementation owes them the protocol, the semantics and — in the places named below — data.


Where that reference is more than reference
-------------------------------------------

Two parts carry material from Mesa rather than only its ideas, and Mesa's MIT notice
(LICENSES/MIT.txt) applies to them:

  - src/vrend/tgsi/ — the TGSI opcode table, its dump format and its text parser follow
    src/gallium/auxiliary/tgsi/{tgsi_info,tgsi_dump,tgsi_text,tgsi_scan}.c entry for entry.
    Copyright © 2008 VMware, Inc. (and Tungsten Graphics).

  - src/vrend/formats.rs — the format tables are generated at build time from Mesa's
    u_format.yaml and from virglrenderer's virgl_hw.h, both in the pinned C tree.


